WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.100
Leaders bring out the best in us.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:14.600
(Casting)

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.300
They push us beyond our limits.

00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:17.640
Isolate our strengths.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.900
And refine our weaknesses.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:24.400
(Casting)

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.180
Leaders show up when the odds aren’t in our favour.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:30.140
When it feels like all hope is lost.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.040
(Casting)

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.040
They redefine what loyalty means.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.900
They stick it out while their surroundings change, and they

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.420
understand what it means to play as a team.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:47.500
"My goals at the moment are, that we become the best team in the world."

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.920
This is the story of leadership.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.840
The story of perseverance and eventual dominance.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:57.880
The story of becoming the best in the world at what you do.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.040
This, is the story of NiKo.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:08.360
"And Niko, that's the final nail in the coffin."

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:19.360
Nikola "NiKo" Kovač was born on February 16, 1997 in Bosnia and was first exposed to

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:24.110
Counter-Strike as a nine-year-old, when his parents introduced him to net cafes.

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:29.040
From the very beginning, Counter-Strike for Niko was about being better than those around him.

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:34.780
From besting his peers, then building a team of locals and finally in 2013 joining pro

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.720
Counter Strike teams iNation and later Team Refuse.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:44.620
(Casting)

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:50.240
Early on in his career, Niko primarily played with Serbian rosters and was focused on elevating

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:52.939
his region to reach Counter-Strike relevancy.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:58.060
In fact, he wanted to become great with a regional roster so badly, that he declined

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.000
an offer to join mousesports

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.420
"When I was turning 18 I got my first offer from Mousesports which I declined.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:08.320
I still believe I can make it to the top with a Serbian team.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:12.040
I did not tell it to my parents because I know they would force me to

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.180
to accept the offer.

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:15.980
Because they knew that I wanted this since I was a kid."

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:20.760
But despite playing on a number of different rosters, he was never able to find the level of

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.520
success he craved.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:27.920
He knew he wanted to be the best, and quickly realized that he couldn’t do that in Bosnia.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:33.480
So after two years playing competitively with regional rosters — Niko accepted a second

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:37.080
offer from mousesports on March 4th 2015.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:42.920
"Now they enter ESL One Cologne with the biggest gun of them all. Boasting the mighty Niko,

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:46.280
considered by some to be the best player in Counter-Strike.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:51.440
During his transition to mouz, Niko was known as a promising young talent and garnered a

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:54.660
reputation as the region’s top prospect.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:03:09.220
(Casting)

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:13.940
Mouz was largely in a developmental phase during Niko’s first year as the team lacked

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:16.800
the fire power necessary to compete with the best.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:21.560
But Niko was proving that he was more than capable of rifling with the scene’s best,

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:26.420
and as we’ve come to learn — the Bosnian marksman had an extraordinary ability to secure

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:30.160
Frags with a Deagle, or just about any other weapon.

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:46.340
(Casting)

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:51.820
In an effort to shake up their lineup, Mouz dropped Gob B in December of 2015, the team’s

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.300
primary shot caller.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:58.360
Which placed a metaphorical Captain’s crest on Niko’s chest heading into the new year

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.200
and the next era  of mousesports.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:13.780
(Casting)

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:18.720
And as January came around, mousesports were more or less the Niko show.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:27.960
(Casting)

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:33.400
But while Niko continued to wow the CS:GO community, Mouz were still a middle of the pack team.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:40.560
(Casting)

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:46.160
During the beginning of their 2016 campaign they finished 5/6 at DreamHack Open Leipzig,

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:52.380
won Acer Predator Masters Season 2, placed 9-12 at the MLG Major in Columbus and 8th

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:55.020
at ESL Pro League Europe Season 3.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:05:00.180
Even throughout their flashes of brilliance it was always Niko clutching the round.

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:02.540
Niko stealing the show.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:08.160
And Niko dragging his teammates up the treacherous side of the pro CSGO mountain.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:16.920
(Casting)

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:23.040
Mouz were able to qualify for 2016’s second Major — ESL: One Cologne, but they walked

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:26.080
away with a mediocre 9-12 finish.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:31.600
During the event, Niko finished a 1.07 rating and 71 total kills.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:35.960
But again fell short of adding a significant finish to his resume.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:39.220
With that said, the team did rebound from Cologne nicely.

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:42.720
Putting up their most notable finish to-date with Niko on the roster.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:45.560
A semi final exit from ELEAGUE Season 1.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:55.440
(Casting)

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:00.520
Through ESL: One Cologne and ELEAGUE Season 1 the CS world had more or less come to a

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:05.240
consensus that Niko was the world’s greatest
Counter Strike players.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:10.080
But, he was playing on a team that was struggling to hang on to a Top 10 ranking.

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:11.920
"He's one of the best players in the world.

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:16.280
He's got unbelievable aim and probably a really good game sense as well."

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:18.320
(Casting)

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:21.200
But Niko didn’t want to go anywhere.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:25.360
Something that has since become a fixture of his identity as a pro player.

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:29.020
Unlike other star players who are willing to jump ship to chase wins.

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:32.700
Niko has always tried to bring his team up to his level.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.520
Not abandon them.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:37.140
Niko has always been team-first.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:40.680
"You know everyone can say you're the best player or whatever, your team's getting better but,

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:45.800
you have to get to that level sooner, so when should it happen, when is the point when Mousesports

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:46.700
has to perform."

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:52.080
"I think now with ELEAGUE and the Major, I feel that we have to go through the groups to advance to playoffs

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:53.520
and see what we can do there."

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:59.700
Throughout the remainder of 2016, Niko continued to shine bright as the game’s most feared player.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:02.220
But mouz maintained their mediocrity.

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:08.520
They finished 3rd/4th at ESL Pro League Season 4 Finals and then 5-8th at ELEAGUE Season 2.

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:16.100
(Casting)

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:22.660
As the calendar turned and 2017 began, all eyes were on Niko at the ELEAGUE Major: Atlanta

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:27.100
The community agreed that it was time for the world’s best player to add some much

00:07:27.100 --> 00:07:29.620
deserved hardware to his trophy case.

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:33.020
If Niko could fight his way out, Mouz had a chance.

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:38.080
But not even the best in the game could carry his team out of the hole they dug him into.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:39.960
"I think all of a sudden you have a situation where,

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:42.240
nothing seems to be going right for NiKo and I think

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:44.960
now we're starting to see him kind of buckle under the pressure.

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:47.640
Having to be the star player and at points having to be the in-game leader."

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:52.840
To say that ELEAGUE Atlanta was a disappointment would be a dramatic understatement.

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:57.020
Mouz finished 12-14th and didn’t make it past the Group Stage.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:08:03.080
"Absolutely heartbreaking, they end up on Nuke and they did not look like a team that were prepared for it at all."

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:07.420
"It's one of the more devastating losses that we've seen here, obviously it's devastating you've lost

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:12.080
you're out of the tournament, but I don't think anybody on Mousesports can say they performed up to

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:15.500
the level they needed, and probably that they thought they could bring on Nuke."

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:28.000
It was clear that the Bosnian superstar needed to make a change to live up to his immense potential,

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:33.000
and on February 9, 2017 Niko left mousesports.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:38.540
Despite his desire to stick it out with mousesports, Niko packed his bags and left for FaZe Clan.

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:42.400
A move that was nothing short of a blockbuster signing.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:47.040
"Well speaking of leaving the team as you just mentioned you will be joining FaZe after this event

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:50.640
How excited are you and what are your expectations joining this new team."

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:55.200
"I'm really looking forward to this, it's been long time since I wanted to play with them,

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:59.400
like maybe, especially with Rain cause I really like that player. So,

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:03.880
I don't know I think our goal is going to be to reach top 1 and that's it."

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:09.760
FaZe already had its star power in Karrigan and mixing superstars in pro CS was and still

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:11.280
is a big risk.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:13.040
But, as we know now.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:15.780
FaZe and Niko were the perfect match.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:21.060
"But now with the most recent addition of Niko, they're actually looking like a team who can be a contender for

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:22.980
championships moving into the future."

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:28.460
Niko, KioShima, Allu, Karrigan and rain began their journey together with their first premier

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:31.220
event at Starladder Season 3.

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:33.760
And they made their presence felt immediately.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:46.480
(Casting)

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:52.000
FaZe Clan defeated the likes of SK Gaming, G2 Esports and Hellraisers to find themselves

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:55.840
in the finals, their first big splash with Niko on the roster.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:06.720
(Casting)

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:09.360
FaZe met Astralis in the grand final.

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:13.400
And it was time that Niko showed the world that he could perform when there was some

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:15.000
hardware on the line.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:11:04.780
(Casting)

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:09.380
Niko had finally landed somewhere where the supporting cast wasn’t blinded

00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:11.560
by him being the game’s brightest star.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:18.280
And now, with winning on their mind, Niko and FaZe Clan had their eyes set on a Major title.

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:28.000
But, Krakow wasn’t the place for Niko’s destiny to be realized.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:33.780
FaZe Clan didn’t even make it out of groups and even worse, were bested by Niko’s former team,

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:34.840
mousesports.

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:41.320
"That has to be, highest expectations, and worse outcome that I've seen in recent memory at a Major."

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:46.420
The community had high hopes for FaZe to make a run and prove themselves in Krakow,

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:48.540
but they still had a long way to go.

00:11:48.660 --> 00:12:03.000
(Casting)

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:06.180
They were close, but something else needed to change

00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:09.660
in order for them to reach the upper echelon of CS:GO.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:14.180
And what happened next, blew the lid off of the Counter Strike scene.

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:17.760
"GuardiaN has joined FaZe. Replacing Allu."

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:23.500
"When you consider this is a superteam that even in the context of superteams is incredibly stacked,

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:27.480
I mean they have three players who you could make a case at one point in history

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:31.720
were legitimately the best player in the world. They have NiKo, they have Olofmeister, they have GuardiaN."

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:36.600
In the weeks following the Krakow Major FaZe Clan acquired Olofmeister and Guardian,

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:38.820
two of the best players in the world.

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:44.040
These two stars, in conjunction with Niko, Karrigan and Rain became the newest iteration

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:45.230
of FaZe Clan.

00:12:45.230 --> 00:12:47.660
And Niko was the team’s linchpin.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:51.480
"If FaZe run into some problem, I would just look towards NiKo and he'll probably close it down for them."

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:55.160
Now, this new FaZe roster would be a test for Niko.

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:59.700
The traditional idea of leadership that he exemplified with Mouz couldn’t exist while

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:02.000
surrounded by superstars.

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:07.420
All egos would have to pushed aside, and Niko would have to focus on being the young gun

00:13:07.420 --> 00:13:10.440
instead of the team captain for the first time.

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:16.820
This super team iteration of FaZe Clan had only a hand full of premier events to prove themselves before

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:23.000
the next Majorm including ESL One: New York and the 2017 ELEAGUE Premier in Atlanta.

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:25.360
FaZe Clan came.

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:31.980
(Casting)

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:33.440
They saw.

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:42.880
(Casting)

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:44.220
And they conquered.

00:13:44.240 --> 00:14:01.300
(Casting)

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:03.520
Not only did they win both events.

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:08.900
But they made it look easy . Sure, the squad was filled with an obnoxious amount of talent.

00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:14.200
But what was most impressive was their ability to play as a cohesive team together.

00:14:14.740 --> 00:14:25.120
(Casting)

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:30.240
The pressure never rested on just one player’s shoulders, and the team wasn’t dragged kicking

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:33.300
and screaming to glory by a single competitor.

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:37.940
Everyone had one goal in mind — securing trophies.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:41.200
And that goal was realized in back to back events.

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:45.480
"Just an incredible performance, this team is not really that old, they just formed

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:49.960
and usually it takes a while before you get this level, not in this case."

00:14:55.180 --> 00:15:00.720
To say that Niko was integral to the team’s rise to the top would be an understatement..

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:06.260
He sacrificed his frags, his stardom and his stats for the better of the team and set a

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:08.770
new benchmark for what it means to be a leader.

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:12.320
And it’s here where Niko separates himself from the pack.

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:16.360
While other superstar players like s1mple have been mired by instability and claims

00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:19.320
of toxicity — Niko keeps quiet.

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:23.340
His numbers aren’t those of a hard carry, and they might not always jump off the page

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:24.680
at first glance.

00:15:24.680 --> 00:15:27.860
But the wins pile up all the same.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:31.800
The stage was set for the pinnacle of Niko’s career to be reached.

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:36.820
FaZe Clan were the overwhelming favourites to win the Boston Major.

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:40.520
Anything less than first place was simply a failure.

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:45.720
FaZe went 3-1 at the New Challengers stage with significant wins against both Natus

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:47.400
Vincere and Team Liquid.

00:15:47.740 --> 00:15:52.320
Then they swept their way through the New Legends Stage beating Fnatic, Vega Squadron

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:54.400
and the almighty SK Gaming.

00:15:54.400 --> 00:16:01.880
(Casting)

00:16:01.880 --> 00:16:06.520
FaZe Clan were meeting expectations — and the New Champions Stage was set.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:09.960
First up was a revamped version of Niko’s former team.

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:13.180
This time though, the Bosnian got the better of mousesports.

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:34.560
(Casting)

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:38.520
Next FaZe met s1mple and Natus Vincere in the semifinals.

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:42.240
A team of superstars against one of the scene’s deadliest players.

00:16:42.240 --> 00:17:00.100
(Casting)

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:04.640
Not only did FaZe put up another 2-0 sweep, but Niko popped off.

00:17:04.640 --> 00:17:09.180
He finished with a +20 over the two games and a 1.51 rating.

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:12.840
Niko’s eyes were now set on the game’s top prize.

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:19.560
"Ladies and gentlemen, welcome to the ELEAGUE Major: Boston."

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:29.400
The stage was set for a David vs. Goliath-esque finals as FaZe Clan’s super team were set

00:17:29.419 --> 00:17:34.129
to take on a young Cloud9 squad that were hungry to become the first North American

00:17:34.129 --> 00:17:37.180
Counter Strike franchise to win a Major.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:18:36.400
(Casting)

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:41.480
The series went to a game three. Inferno. For a Major title.

00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:48.120
"I can't wait to see, what these teams have to offer us here on Inferno. FaZe Clan on the CT side, Cloud9 will

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:51.040
will start as they mean to go as the aggressors."

00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:54.800
"Boston makes some noise in this b*tch!"

00:18:55.480 --> 00:19:00.860
C9 were playing out of their minds, and early in Game three FaZe was having trouble keeping up.

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:16.120
(Casting)

00:19:16.120 --> 00:19:20.940
As with all great stories of competition, this one went into overtime.

00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:41.520
(Casting)

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:46.480
In overtime, Cloud9 made it clear that they were not going to lay down and let FaZe Clan

00:19:46.480 --> 00:19:48.160
complete a comeback victory.

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:53.460
C9 took the first three rounds to open up an 18-15 lead.

00:19:53.460 --> 00:20:02.460
(Casting)

00:20:02.520 --> 00:20:04.120
But FaZe responded.

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:07.520
Rattling off four of their own round wins consecutively.

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:25.960
(Casting)

00:20:26.560 --> 00:20:28.800
And then – heartbreak.

00:20:28.880 --> 00:21:13.080
(Casting)

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:23.840
In the wake of landing on the unfortunate side of Cloud9’s historic run, FaZe Clan

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:28.480
has more or less maintained their stranglehold as one of the best teams in the game.

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:34.100
Niko is still considered one of the best players in the game alongside the likes of s1mple and Coldzera.

00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:38.940
And this still may be the most intimidating roster in the game’s history.

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:42.980
But as with anything in esports, things are constantly in flux.

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:48.460
Olofmeister had taken a series of breaks from competitive play, returning to FaZe full time in July.

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:53.080
Astralis meanwhile had taken over the throne as the number one ranked team in the world

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:55.680
with s1mple and Na’vi nipping at their heels

00:21:55.680 --> 00:21:58.419
But, even though FaZe aren’t untouchable.

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:03.240
They’ve still proven to be the same lethal force when their stars align.

00:22:03.240 --> 00:22:08.799
Even without OlofMeister at ESL One: Belo Horizonte Niko and company were able to take

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:10.280
the first place prize.

00:22:10.280 --> 00:22:14.820
Sending a message to the rest of the community that they were nothing to scoff at when major

00:22:14.820 --> 00:22:16.560
season comes back around.

00:22:16.720 --> 00:22:34.040
(Casting)

00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:38.340
As the FACEIT London Major loomed in late September 2018.

00:22:38.340 --> 00:22:43.760
Olof returned to FaZe Clan and Niko and company had another shot to make history.

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:50.720
With their hopes for Major glory in the balance — FaZe tripped out of the gate to an 0-2 start in the group stage.

00:22:50.720 --> 00:23:07.540
(Casting)

00:23:07.540 --> 00:23:11.500
But as we know, champions don't quit when the odds are against them.

00:23:11.500 --> 00:23:21.700
(Casting)

00:23:21.700 --> 00:23:28.060
Niko and FaZe clan rallied off three consecutive victories to find themselves qualified for the elimination rounds.

00:23:28.180 --> 00:23:33.660
In the quarterfinals, FaZe would face maybe their toughest challenge since Boston — Astralis,

00:23:33.680 --> 00:23:35.280
the world’s top ranked team.

00:23:35.360 --> 00:23:42.440
"Ladies and gentlemen, bring the noise for Astralis and the FaZe Clan."

00:23:43.160 --> 00:23:44.880
The match was a war.

00:23:44.880 --> 00:24:54.840
(Casting)

00:24:54.840 --> 00:25:00.280
Another chance to seal the letter on a storied career for Niko. And another bracket exit.

00:25:04.480 --> 00:25:08.240
From staying loyal in Bosnia, to trying to make it work with mousesports

00:25:08.240 --> 00:25:10.840
and coming so close with FaZe Clan

00:25:10.980 --> 00:25:14.420
Niko has become a household name in the CS:GO scene.

00:25:14.420 --> 00:25:19.540
There aren’t that many win/loss metrics that separate the best players in Counter Strike,

00:25:19.540 --> 00:25:23.440
but above all else the ability to take home that Major trophy

00:25:23.440 --> 00:25:25.960
can make or break the legacy of a career

00:25:26.360 --> 00:25:32.520
And for someone as bent on greatness as Niko — nothing short of a Major winning moment will do.

00:25:32.740 --> 00:25:37.140
"I really love what I'm doing and I'm going to try and play as long as I can,

00:25:37.140 --> 00:25:43.040
I don't know what my family will say at the end of my career, but I believe that they're gonna be really proud."

00:25:43.460 --> 00:25:46.580
To prove what it means to be the best in the game.

00:25:46.640 --> 00:25:52.240
That it takes loyalty, teamwork and sacrifice, the things he’s branded himself on.

00:25:52.720 --> 00:25:54.380
The consummate professional.

00:25:54.500 --> 00:25:55.440
The leader.

00:25:55.440 --> 00:25:56.400
The captain.

00:25:56.760 --> 00:25:57.800
The Superstar.

00:25:59.640 --> 00:26:00.520
NiKo.

00:26:04.960 --> 00:26:09.780
Thanks for watching. If you want more great content just like this, be sure to hit the subscribe button.

